---
// src/pages/legal/privacy-policy.astro
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Ember Ridge, a ministry of Firebrand Revivalists, collects, uses, shares, and protects information submitted through this website."
  updated="30 July 2026"
  intro="We treat what is shared with this ministry — especially personal circumstances and requests for prayer — with care and restraint."
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Ember Ridge is a ministry of Firebrand Revivalists, a church within the meaning of
    section 508(c)(1)(A) of the Internal Revenue Code, located in Moravian Falls, North
    Carolina (“we,” “us,” “our,” “the ministry”). This policy explains how we handle
    information collected through this website.
  </p>
  <p>
    Questions, requests, and complaints may be sent to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This policy applies to this website. It does not apply to third-party services that
    operate under their own policies, including the giving platforms listed on our
    Partner page. When you follow a link to one of those services, their privacy
    practices govern.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is directed to visitors in the United States. We do not target our
    services to individuals in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Information we collect</h2>

  <h3>Information you provide</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name and email address</li>
    <li>Your church, ministry, or organization, if you choose to give it</li>
    <li>Your stated reason for contacting us</li>
    <li>The content of your message</li>
    <li>Whether you asked that your message be handled confidentially</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A message may contain sensitive details — including health, family, or financial
    circumstances — because you chose to include them. We ask that you send only what is
    necessary. Information relating to physical or mental health is also governed by our
    <a href="/legal/consumer-health-data-privacy">Consumer Health Data Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider records standard server information such as IP address, browser
    and device type, referring page, pages requested, and date and time. This is used for
    security, spam prevention, troubleshooting, and understanding general site usage.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site does not use analytics software, advertising technology, social media
    trackers, or third-party fonts. We do not build visitor profiles.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To read and respond to your message</li>
    <li>To pray for needs you ask us to carry</li>
    <li>To evaluate partnership, referral, and placement inquiries</li>
    <li>To acknowledge and receipt gifts, and to maintain donor records</li>
    <li>To maintain records appropriate to a church and its ministries</li>
    <li>To operate, secure, and improve this website</li>
    <li>To comply with law, and to establish or defend legal claims</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. What we do not do</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information. We do not share personal information for
    cross-context behavioral advertising. We do not rent, trade, or otherwise disclose
    contact information to unrelated organizations. We do not use the content of
    prayer requests or personal correspondence in public teaching, publications, or
    fundraising material without permission.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Confidentiality of requests for prayer and counsel</h2>
  <p>
    Messages are read by ministry leadership. Requests for prayer may be shared with the
    intercession team unless you ask that your message be limited to leadership. Members
    of the intercession team serving in a sustained capacity are subject to written
    confidentiality expectations.
  </p>
  <p>
    This website is not a secure channel. Please do not transmit medical records,
    financial account numbers, government identification numbers, or other highly
    sensitive records through it.
  </p>

  <h2>7. When we disclose information</h2>
  <p>We disclose personal information only as follows:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers.</strong> Vendors that operate this website and deliver
      messages to us — currently our website host and form processor, and our email
      provider. They process information on our behalf and are not permitted to use it
      for their own purposes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Professional advisors.</strong> Attorneys, accountants, auditors, and
      insurers, where reasonably necessary.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal requirements.</strong> Where required by law, subpoena, or other
      legal process, or where we believe in good faith that disclosure is necessary to
      protect the safety of any person, to prevent harm, or to protect our rights.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Successors.</strong> In connection with a merger, consolidation, or
      transfer of ministry assets, subject to this policy.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. How long we keep information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>General correspondence:</strong> up to twenty-four months from your last contact, then deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Prayer requests:</strong> retained only as long as needed to serve the request, and not longer than twenty-four months.</li>
    <li><strong>Giving and donor records:</strong> retained as required for tax, accounting, and audit purposes, generally seven years.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> retained by our host on its standard schedule, generally no more than thirty days.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may retain information longer where necessary to comply with law or to establish
    or defend a legal claim.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>
  <p>
    This site is served over encrypted connections (HTTPS). Access to submissions is
    limited to leadership and to team members with a specific reason to see them. No
    method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee
    absolute security.
  </p>
  <p>
    If a security incident affecting personal information occurs, we will provide notice
    as required by applicable law, including the North Carolina Identity Theft Protection
    Act and the Washington data breach notification statute.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>You may ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Confirm whether we hold information about you, and provide a copy</li>
    <li>Correct information that is inaccurate</li>
    <li>Delete information we hold about you</li>
    <li>Stop contacting you</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Send your request to <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
    We will respond within forty-five days. If we need additional time, we will tell you
    why and how long we expect to take. We will not deny you service or treat you
    differently for exercising these rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    If we decline a request, you may appeal by replying to our response and asking for
    reconsideration. We will respond to an appeal within forty-five days and, if we again
    decline, explain why.
  </p>

  <h3>Washington residents</h3>
  <p>
    Washington has not enacted a comprehensive consumer privacy statute. Information
    relating to your physical or mental health is governed by the Washington My Health My
    Data Act, and your rights under that law — including the right to withdraw consent
    and the right to have such data deleted — are described in our separate
    <a href="/legal/consumer-health-data-privacy">Consumer Health Data Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>North Carolina residents</h3>
  <p>
    North Carolina has not enacted a comprehensive consumer privacy statute. The rights
    described above are offered to all visitors as a matter of practice.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control</h2>
  <p>
    Because this site does not track visitors across other websites and does not sell or
    share personal information for targeted advertising, there is nothing for a Do Not
    Track or Global Privacy Control signal to switch off. We will honor such signals if
    that ever changes.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information
    from children under 13, consistent with the Children’s Online Privacy Protection Act.
    If you believe a child has submitted information, write to us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The date at the top reflects the current version. Material
    changes will be noted on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Ember Ridge, a ministry of Firebrand Revivalists<br />
    Moravian Falls, North Carolina<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
